Subject: [PATCH 193/260] [ae-patch] Fill a family lead's row and hover cards:
 name room, a folded count badge, open sessions, raises and closed rows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lead rows held 16px for a thinking spinner even when idle, so the name stopped about 28px short. The spinner now takes the time's place (left of it only when the time slot holds another marker), so an idle row's title runs to the time. A folded lead's chevron carries its open count as a badge on its corner, pink when a hidden session waits on you; the time column never moves.

The lead's hover card reads "3 open · 6 closed", shows tokens and cost as two rows under Spend shows Both, and names up to 4 open sessions with their role and state. A child that started sessions of its own gets the same block for them. A raised helper's card says where it started, when it was raised, whether its cap is reached, and why. Rows under "N closed" get the same hover card as open rows.
